(---) Tj
T*
(Orvan wheat: the sea loss is real, the substitutes are small) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P1] View. We think the market is still underestimating the duration of the) Tj
T*
(Orvan sea disruption.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P2] The corridor agreement ended on 10 September and the port strike began on) Tj
T*
(14 September. The September port index of 40 is the best early guide.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P3] On our numbers, the four main sea routes could lose half to three-fifths of) Tj
T*
(their value in the fourth quarter.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P4] The offsets are real but limited. Rail through Ravik may add about 54% in) Tj
T*
(volume on a base of USD 25M a month.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P5] Vanir wheat sales to Tolan and Midgard may rise by between a seventh and a) Tj
T*
(fifth in volume, again from a small base. The Asgard wheat contract is protected) Tj
T*
(and may lose less than a tenth.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P6] The view rests on three observations. First, the sea route is the cheapest) Tj
T*
(way to move Orvan grain in bulk, so a lasting loss of sea capacity cannot be) Tj
T*
(fully offset by rail or by smaller suppliers. Second, the substitutes are priced) Tj
T*
(at a premium, which supports the price effect even as volumes fall. Third, the) Tj
T*
(protected contract covers only one destination, so it does not change the) Tj
T*
(picture for the open-market routes. We would raise our estimate if the port) Tj
T*
(index stays near its December level into the new year, and lower it if berth use) Tj
T*
(recovers faster than we expect.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P7] The note is deliberately short on price targets. It says the value loss is) Tj
T*
(easier to estimate than the price path, because the port index gives a volume) Tj
T*
(anchor while prices depend on how long the disruption lasts. It expects the) Tj
T*
(price effect to fade before volumes recover, and it will review the view when) Tj
T*
(the port returns to fuller working.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P8] Forecast. We expect the sea index to stay near 30 to 40 through December) Tj
T*
(and to recover only slowly.) Tj
T*
() Tj
